      "writtenOn": "2024-08-19T21:00:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why is this stuff happening in this state and not `SRC_ATTACHED_GET_PDOS`?",
      "revId": "8277597edb69913a232981886c84e6e845a4e02d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e5fbe84e_f69b5470",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_power_mgmt.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1447,
      "author": {
        "id": 1529538
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-20T11:01:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The variable is used as the pdos to be retrieved so initializing it before entering the *_ATTACHED_GET_PDOS state and updating the value in *_ATTACHED_GET_PDOS makes it easier.",
      "parentUuid": "43c03202_61994381",
      "revId": "8277597edb69913a232981886c84e6e845a4e02d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5ac56413_7bc21e1e",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_power_mgmt.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1447,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-20T17:39:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ack. I think this is stretching the usefulness of the substate progression, but I don\u0027t have a better way of doing it that wouldn\u0027t be a significant refactor. Each of these substates initializes port state and then takes some action based on that state. This CL breaks the pattern by relying on state that was initialized in a previous run of the same substate, but it\u0027s the pattern that\u0027s unusual and limiting.\n\nIf you were inclined to clean it up, the first thing that comes to mind to me is that it would make more sense to initialize the port state in `pdc_src_attached_entry`. That would make the substate behavior much less vulnerable to dependency on the order of the substates. But that\u0027s probably out of scope for this CL.\n\nFor now, the placement of this initialization is unexpected and unexpectedly critical to correct operation. I\u0027d suggest a comment explaining why it\u0027s here.",
      "parentUuid": "e5fbe84e_f69b5470",
      "revId": "8277597edb69913a232981886c84e6e845a4e02d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
