      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-19T21:00:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This changes the port state regardless of the result of the command. Will the port state be internally consistent if the command fails?",
      "revId": "8277597edb69913a232981886c84e6e845a4e02d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "58592c40_8e8fe39a",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_power_mgmt.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1739,
      "author": {
        "id": 1529538
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-20T11:01:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks. I think we should validate the rv before moving to next pdos, but probably we need a retry count to avoid blocking in this state if keeping failed ?",
      "parentUuid": "8323dde7_b915e36b",
      "revId": "8277597edb69913a232981886c84e6e845a4e02d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dfe44857_16413daf",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_power_mgmt.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1739,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-20T17:39:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If this fails, I don\u0027t think we have any reason (yet) to believe that a retry might succeed, and the next set of PDOs wouldn\u0027t be useful by themselves. For now, let\u0027s just go to error recovery and see what the PDC does.",
      "parentUuid": "58592c40_8e8fe39a",
      "revId": "8277597edb69913a232981886c84e6e845a4e02d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0c6e3b70_9a89358a",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_power_mgmt.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1742,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-19T21:00:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This code is a bit complicated to read, and it checks `pdo_nums` twice. I think that could be avoided by using some variables at the beginning of this case.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1732,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1742,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "8277597edb69913a232981886c84e6e845a4e02d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e23132f3_b3714b31",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_power_mgmt.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1742,
      "author": {
        "id": 1529538
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-20T11:01:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since pdo_nums and pdo_offset are used as params in UCSI command, so they have to be updated accordingly while determining the re-entrance of *_ATTACHED_GET_PDOS. Since it is not possible to use one variable to identify if we are going to enter another SRC or SNK_ATTACHED_GET_PDOS and get_pdo.pdo_nums is the shared variable could be used, I think it would be simpler rather than create an additional variable just for check.",
      "parentUuid": "0c6e3b70_9a89358a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1732,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1742,
        "endChar": 3
